<onlyinclude>'''Conway's Game of Life''' is a two-dimensional cellular automaton devised by John Horton Conway and publicized by Martin Gardner in 1970. A grid of cells repeatedly changes between live and dead states according to fixed local rules.

== Explanation ==
A live cell survives with two or three live neighbors; a dead cell becomes live with exactly three. All other cells become or remain dead. Starting patterns may disappear, stay unchanged, repeat or move across the grid. Despite its name, the cells are mathematical states, not biological organisms.

